recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two questions, both cheap to answer and neither mine. %574 still stands where the last lap left it: may a lap correct its own grader, when the fix re-grades every page unmeasured? And the boundary I proposed puts the page I just wrote on the wrong side of itself -- running-the-fleet.md is operator prose in the shipping room, one file with three inbound links, so moving it later costs almost nothing if you seat the boundary as measured.
